# Fieldset

A fieldset gives several controls one shared question or purpose.

These are civica reference implementations for component authors. They do not replace native Home Assistant behaviour or demonstrate a connection to a live home.

## When to use it

Use it for room checkboxes, an exclusive display choice, or the three parts of a date. Its legend names the group; individual labels still describe each input.

## When not to use it

Do not use a fieldset as a decorative box around unrelated settings or readings. A collection of sensor values is usually a summary list or table, not a form group.

## Home Assistant adaptation

For a dashboard editor, separate display choices from integration settings so the legend describes a coherent task. On a one-question page the legend can contain the page heading. In a multi-section settings page use the appropriate lower heading level instead of repeating h1.

## Accessibility and behaviour

Place the legend first and keep it short because a screen reader may repeat it for each control. Associate a short group hint programmatically. Native Home Assistant components may expose their own grouping semantics; check the rendered accessibility tree before adding wrappers.

